1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:00,700
Hi.

2
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:02,810
So good to see you again.

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:07,010
In this lesson, we're going to talk about companies.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:12,620
Types of companies and how to make questions in English.

5
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:13,730
All right.

6
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:18,600
First, let's have a look at types of worker.

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,710
So you can work as a freelancer.

8
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:30,320
That means that you work per task or project and you get paid for an hour of work or accomplished.

9
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:31,130
Task.

10
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:33,610
Or you can be an employee.

11
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:36,980
That means that you are a part of a company.

12
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:46,850
You do different tasks and have different responsibilities and you get fixed salary plus some benefits.

13
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:48,720
All right.

14
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:57,660
So companies in it are divided into two main types first type product company.

15
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:03,240
This company develops one or several connected products.

16
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:12,090
And if you work there, you work on one project or similar projects during your career in this company.

17
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:18,990
Service company has different clients and develops many different projects for them.

18
00:01:18,990 --> 00:01:24,660
And if you work there, you can switch projects and clients more often.

19
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:33,010
Okay examples of this companies product company, for example, Airbnb.

20
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:41,650
Their product is a platform where you can find and rent an apartment and service company.

21
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,660
For example, global logic.

22
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:49,060
They have many different clients and they develop many different project for them.

23
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:58,940
Let's have a look at how companies describe themselves and try to guess the type of a company.

24
00:01:59,630 --> 00:02:00,800
First company.

25
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:08,930
We deliver business and technology transformation from start to finish using Agile methodologies, proven

26
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:16,580
customer collaboration approach, engineering excellence tools, hybrid teams, and our award winning

27
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,410
global delivery platform.

28
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:19,780
All right.

29
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:27,560
We see words like deliver business from start to finish and customer.

30
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:32,090
That means this is a service company.

31
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,940
Second at ABC Company.

32
00:02:36,950 --> 00:02:41,810
We want to help people understand one another better when they communicate.

33
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:49,850
Every day, 30 million people around the world use our product to strengthen their writing and say what

34
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:51,200
they really mean.

35
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:57,380
Here we see phrases like 30 million people use our product.

36
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:02,780
So here is the focus on the product and number of users.

37
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,930
So this is a product company.

38
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:07,740
Next one.

39
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:15,350
We are digital advisors and providers who operate at the cutting edge of technology.

40
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:22,070
We deliver the innovation, quality and speed that our clients expect.

41
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:28,430
Again, we see words like clients deliver digital advisors.

42
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:33,080
So here we talk about a service company.

43
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:33,750
Okay.

44
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:40,860
In a service company, the focus is on the client delivery advice.

45
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:46,380
In a product company, the focus is on product users.

46
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:47,340
Good.

47
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,530
Okay.

48
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:51,240
Size of the company.

49
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:53,700
We can have a micro company.

50
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,500
Small company.

51
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:59,100
Middle company and big company.

52
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:08,550
Let's see, what are the advantages and disadvantages of working in a small or big company?

53
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:18,450
So in a small company you can have a wide range of experience, so you can try different roles and responsibilities.

54
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:21,720
Involvement in company mission.

55
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:28,620
So you can suggest some improvements, some innovations.

56
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:37,160
You can make work friends at a small company, but there are some disadvantages, minuses, unknown

57
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:41,000
reputation and culture, limited growth.

58
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:47,210
And due to a lower budget, sometimes not so many benefits.

59
00:04:47,810 --> 00:04:50,060
Advantages of a big company.

60
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:52,950
It's a good start in career.

61
00:04:52,970 --> 00:04:57,350
More room for growth and better process.

62
00:04:57,350 --> 00:05:06,500
But sometimes you might have limited responsibilities and longer process paperwork and bureaucracy.

63
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,160
All right.

64
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,050
Meet my friend Sarah.

65
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,270
She has a new job.

66
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:16,680
I want to find out more about her new company.

67
00:05:16,690 --> 00:05:20,890
So I sent her a message with some questions.

68
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:23,050
All right.

69
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:25,900
I want to know the name of her new company.

70
00:05:26,170 --> 00:05:28,870
A number of people working there.

71
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:32,140
I want to know, how old is her company?

72
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:34,810
The location of main office.

73
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:35,830
And I know.

74
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:40,030
I want to know the name of the person who runs this company.

75
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:42,100
So I make questions.

76
00:05:42,430 --> 00:05:45,280
What is the name of your new company?

77
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:47,500
How many people work there?

78
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:50,380
When was this company founded?

79
00:05:50,410 --> 00:05:53,380
Where is the main office of your company?

80
00:05:53,410 --> 00:05:57,100
Who is the CEO of your company?

81
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:58,170
All right.

82
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:01,750
Pause the video and repeat the questions.

83
00:06:03,650 --> 00:06:04,770
Good job, guys.

84
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:06,650
Now it's your turn.

85
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:13,790
Pause the video again and try to recreate the questions by putting missing words there.

86
